 raised and $20 million on hand, while Whatley has raised about $11 million. Recent polling shows Cooper leading by 7 to 14 points, including surveys from Republican-leaning firms, and prediction markets put his win odds near 95 percent.\n\nThe race's trajectory has worsened for Whatley: his campaign went dark on television in mid-October and GOP outside groups have pulled advertising from the state. Expert raters broadly place the race at Likely D or better, with two calling it Lean D and one Safe D. The state's near-even partisan lean makes Cooper's margin notable, suggesting a candidate-specific advantage rather than pure environment. A late Whatley resurgence or ad resumption remains the main path to a closer finish.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9425, "margin": 7.94}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.93, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9375, "margin": 8.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9346, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9278, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9264, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.939, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9386, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9577, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9557, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9557, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9512, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9379, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9381, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.956, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9414, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9393, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.9452, "margin": 9.2}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.9528, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.965, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_d